{#
	Pick a template, pick a format, get a document.

	One form, rendered twice: inside the modal on the record page, and on its own
	page for whoever arrives without JavaScript. A plain GET form, so the browser
	builds the URL and nothing here needs a script to work — which is also why the
	download route takes its template and format as query parameters.

	A select rather than a row of buttons because a contact may have fifty
	templates, and fifty buttons is the layout this replaced.

	**And whatever the module offers to put on the PDF** (XIV-164), as one tick
	each. This form knows nothing about invoices or payment slips: it draws the
	list the module answered with, in the module's own words, and a module with
	nothing to add turns this back into the form it was before.
#}
<form method="get" action="{{ path('module_document', {module: module.key, id: record.id}) }}"
      data-controller="document-decorations">
	<div class="mb-3">
		<label class="form-label" for="{{ id|default('document') }}-template">{{ 'document.template'|trans }}</label>
		<select class="form-select" id="{{ id|default('document') }}-template" name="template" required>
			{% for template in templates %}
				<option value="{{ template.id }}">{{ template.name }}</option>
			{% endfor %}
		</select>
	</div>

	<div class="mb-3">
		<label class="form-label" for="{{ id|default('document') }}-format">{{ 'document.format'|trans }}</label>
		<select class="form-select" id="{{ id|default('document') }}-format" name="format"
		        data-document-decorations-target="format"
		        data-action="change->document-decorations#refresh">
			{% for format in formats %}
				<option value="{{ format.value }}">{{ ('document.format_' ~ format.value)|trans }}</option>
			{% endfor %}
		</select>
	</div>

	{#
		Ticked, because the slip is the normal case for a Swiss invoice and
		leaving it out is the exception (XIV-164). The known cost of a default
		that is almost always right is that people stop reading it; what changes
		is that the choice exists, and exists where the document is produced.

		Nothing is drawn at all when the list is empty, which covers three cases
		with one silence: a module with no decoration, a tenant whose settings
		could not produce one, and the .docx, which is never decorated. The last
		of those is decided while somebody is standing here rather than before
		the page was built, so the controller on the form hides these again when
		the format changes.
	#}
	{% for decoration in decorations|default([]) %}
		<div class="mb-3 form-check" data-document-decorations-target="field">
			<input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" checked
			       id="{{ id|default('document') }}-decoration-{{ decoration.key }}"
			       name="decorations[]" value="{{ decoration.key }}">
			<label class="form-check-label" for="{{ id|default('document') }}-decoration-{{ decoration.key }}">
				{{ decoration.label|trans }}
			</label>
			{% if decoration.help %}
				<div class="form-text">{{ decoration.help|trans }}</div>
			{% endif %}
		</div>
	{% endfor %}

	<button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">
		<i class="bi bi-download" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ 'document.download'|trans }}
	</button>
</form>
